## 📌 Overview

In an ICU, patients need constant observation. This project uses an **ESP32** microcontroller with biomedical and environmental sensors to measure heart rate, SpO₂, and temperature. Readings are shown locally on a **16x2 LCD** and sent over Wi-Fi to **ThingSpeak**, where they can be viewed as live graphs from anywhere.

## ✨ Features

- Real-time heart rate and SpO₂ monitoring
- Temperature and pressure sensing
- Local display on a 16x2 LCD
- Wireless data upload to the ThingSpeak cloud
- Live graphs and data logging for remote viewing
- Low cost, compact, and easy to extend
- Stable 5V supply using a 7805 voltage regulator

